# Quality gate (before every commit / push)

Agents must verify the **full CI quality bar** before committing. Do not rely on “it looked fine” or unit tests alone.

## Mandatory before every commit

Run from repo root (even for docs/chore/cursor-only diffs):

```bash
npm run format:check
npm run lint
```

If `format:check` fails:

```bash
npm run format
npm run format:check
```

Then include the formatted files in the same commit. Never leave Prettier-dirty files staged or unstaged that CI will scan (`prettier --check .`).

## Also run when the change touches that area

```bash
npm run typecheck          # TS / packages / shared types
npm run test:packages      # api-client / contract
npm run test:api           # apps/api unit
npm run test:api:e2e       # HTTP routes / auth / contracts
npm run test:e2e           # user-facing web / i18n
```

Do not push with red lint, format, typecheck, or tests. Behavior change ⇒ tests in the same change set (see testing rule).

## Why this exists

CI job `quality` runs `format:check` → `lint` → `typecheck`. A single dirty file (including under `.cursor/`) fails the job and **skips** `api-test` / `web-e2e`. Local green unit tests do not mean CI green.

## Diff hygiene — reject leftover process junk

Remove before commit:

- `console.log` / `debugger` / temporary scaffolding
- Commented-out code and dead exports
- Unused imports / speculative deps
- Orphan experiment files
- Secrets, `.env`, credentials, personal paths
- Drive-by reformatting of unrelated files (except when fixing format:check)

## Consistency

- Match existing folder patterns
- Same problem → same solution (auth, validation, storage, i18n, api-client)
- After contract changes: `npm run build:packages` and update callers

## Performance sanity

- No unbounded `findMany` / unpaginated feeds
- No repeated identical fetches in a loop
- Images/files via StorageService / established upload paths

## PR / commit shape

- One concern per commit when practical (Conventional Commits)
- Prefer small PRs over “redesign everything” dumps
